{"name":"Federation of Love","hex":"#b71010","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"federation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of joining together into a single political entity.","An array of nations or states that are unified under one central authority."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of an architectural style popular around the time of federation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/federation"},{"term":"love","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A deep caring for the existence of another.","Strong affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To have a strong affection for (someone or something).","To need, thrive on."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/love"}],"entries":[{"title":"Federation","blocks":[{"text":"A federation is a union of partially self-governing provinces, states, or other regions under a federal government (federalism). In a federation, the self-governing status of the component units and the division of power between them and the central government are constitutionally entrenched and may not be altered unilaterally by either the central or constituent-unit authorities without following the constitutional amendment process."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Map_of_unitary_and_federal_states.svg/330px-Map_of_unitary_and_federal_states.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federation"},{"title":"Love","blocks":[{"text":"Love encompasses a range of strong and positive emotional and mental states, from the most sublime virtue or good habit, the deepest interpersonal affection, to the simplest pleasure. An example of this range of meanings is that the love of a mother differs from the love of a spouse, which differs from the love for food. Most commonly, love refers to a feeling of strong attraction and emotional attachment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Love"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Nigeria_states.png/500px-Nigeria_states.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Nigeria_states.png/500px-Nigeria_states.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" A map of the Federal Republic of Nigeria, showing its 36 states and the Federal Capital Territory","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANigeria_states.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Np.png/500px-Np.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Np.png/1280px-Np.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Np.png/500px-Np.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map of the Federal Democratic Republic of Nepal showing its seven constituent provinces","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANp.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Malaysia_states_named.png/500px-Malaysia_states_named.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Malaysia_states_named.png/1280px-Malaysia_states_named.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Malaysia_states_named.png/500px-Malaysia_states_named.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map of Malaysia showing its thirteen states and three federal territories","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMalaysia_states_named.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Cart